  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "A typical Hindi sentence has three basic parts. The verb comes last, the subject first, and the rest in between.\nयह बम्बई है ।\nइसका नाम क्या है ।\nThe subject does not have to be stated; the first three sentences above illustrate this. Subject and verb only make a complete sentence, as in the last three. The verb by itself can be a sentence."
